{
  "question": "Using official PostgreSQL documentation, explain what the uuidv7() function added in PostgreSQL 18 does and how it differs from uuidv4(). Include limitations and avoid unsupported performance claims.",
  "language": "en",
  "title": "Comparison of uuidv7() and uuidv4() Functions in PostgreSQL 18",
  "banner": null,
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "summary",
      "title": "Summary",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "PostgreSQL provides native support for generating UUIDs using the UUIDv4 and UUIDv7 algorithms.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "labels": [
            "single_source"
          ],
          "findings": [
            "k11"
          ],
          "sources": [
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "While uuidv4() generates random identifiers, the uuidv7() function introduced in PostgreSQL 18 creates time-ordered, sortable UUIDs.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "labels": [
            "single_source"
          ],
          "findings": [
            "k4",
            "k5",
            "k7"
          ],
          "sources": [
            2,
            3,
            4
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "key_findings",
      "title": "Key Findings",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "The uuidv7() function generates a version 7 time-ordered UUID using a UNIX timestamp with millisecond precision, sub-millisecond timestamp data, and random bits.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "labels": [],
          "findings": [
            "k1",
            "k5"
          ],
          "sources": [
            2,
            3,
            5
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "According to a single source, uuidv7() embeds the current time at the beginning to ensure sortability, and monotonicity is ensured within the same backend.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "labels": [
            "single_source"
          ],
          "findings": [
            "k7",
            "k8"
          ],
          "sources": [
            4
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The native UUID type supported UUIDv4 generation prior to PostgreSQL 18, and the uuidv4() function generates a version 4 random UUID.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "labels": [
            "single_source"
          ],
          "findings": [
            "k4",
            "k9"
          ],
          "sources": [
            2,
            4
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A single source notes that UUIDv4 values are not monotonic, whereas UUIDv7 values are sortable.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "labels": [
            "single_source"
          ],
          "findings": [
            "k10"
          ],
          "sources": [
            4
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The uuid_extract_timestamp() function solely supports extracting timestamps from version 1 or 7 UUIDs, returning null for other versions.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "labels": [
            "single_source"
          ],
          "findings": [
            "k2"
          ],
          "sources": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A single source states that a limitation of uuidv7() is that it reveals the approximate creation time, which is a potential privacy concern.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "labels": [
            "single_source"
          ],
          "findings": [
            "k6"
          ],
          "sources": [
            5
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The official documentation for PostgreSQL UUID generation functions is located in Section 9.14 at https://postgresql.org/docs/current/functions-uuid.html.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "labels": [
            "single_source"
          ],
          "findings": [
            "k3",
            "k12"
          ],
          "sources": [
            1,
            2
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "conflicting_or_uncertain",
      "title": "Conflicting / Uncertain Information",
      "sentences": []
    },
    {
      "key": "conclusion",
      "title": "Conclusion",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "The uuidv7() function differs from uuidv4() by embedding a timestamp to produce sortable, monotonic identifiers instead of purely random values.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "labels": [],
          "findings": [
            "k1",
            "k4",
            "k10"
          ],
          "sources": [
            2,
            4,
            5
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Although uuidv7() enables timestamp extraction, a single source highlights that exposing the creation time poses a privacy limitation.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "labels": [
            "single_source"
          ],
          "findings": [
            "k2",
            "k6"
          ],
          "sources": [
            2,
            5
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
